14. Longest Common Prefix
Write a function to find the longest common prefix string amongst an array of strings.
If there is no common prefix, return an empty string "".

Example 1:

Input: strs = ["flower","flow","flight"]
Output: "fl"

Explanation:
Sort the array first. Pick out the first and last element from the array of strings.
looks like flight, flow, flower
start iterating the words, check if first char is same as the last char, if so add it to ans string builder.
else break.

Code:

class Solution {
    public String longestCommonPrefix(String[] strs) {
        StringBuilder ans = new StringBuilder();

        if(strs.length==0){
            return "";
        }

        Arrays.sort(strs);
        String first=strs[0];
        String last=strs[strs.length-1];

        for(int i=0;i<Math.min(first.length(),last.length());i++){
            if(first.charAt(i)==last.charAt(i)){
                ans.append(first.charAt(i));
            }
            else{
                break;
            }
        }
        return ans.toString();
    }
}
